  "title": "Abebe Bikila wins the Rome Olympic marathon barefoot",
  "summary": "On 10 September 1960 Abebe Bikila of Ethiopia won the Olympic marathon in Rome, running barefoot in 2:15:16.2. The course passed the Baths of Caracalla, ran down the Appian Way and finished under the Arch of Constantine, in the dark.",
